Milestone 2 Phase G.6 — Operational Family presence and confidence review
=========================================================================

Date          2026-08-10
Board         Waveshare ESP32-S3-LCD-2.8, non-touch, SKU 30223
Firmware      0.1.0-dev  git=f0edebc  dirty=false  profile=hardware-validation
              image 0xe7780, ESP-IDF v5.5.4, LVGL 9.5.0
Flow          PRD_VALIDATION_OPERATIONAL_WALK with PRD_UI_RENDER_REPORT

Scope         The six Operational Family states plus the three compositions the
              family fixtures cannot reach: Printing at reduced confidence,
              Ready at reduced confidence, and Printing whose record the
              machine never supplied.

Session       50 minutes, 0 -> 3002 s uptime. 33 walk loads: all nine cases
              walked three complete times plus a partial fourth pass.
              0 errors. Flush 238/238, no failures, no deadline misses.
              Button 98 raw edges -> 32 gestures, 0 dropped.

Read this     Each load emits three lines -- the fixture and its projected
              state, the values behind it, and the geometry the renderer
              actually placed -- followed by one layout line per element.
              `present=` on a telemetry row is the Phase G.3 presence rule.
              `base=`/`now=` is the Phase G.1 time base: base == now means the
              board's clock bound, base > now means the previous script's own
              timeline did.

Redaction     Board serial output only. Contains no machine paths, usernames,
              serial numbers, credentials, network names or printer payloads;
              this profile performs no networking. ANSI colour codes stripped.
              Timestamps are seconds since the capture opened the port.

